    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Great Depression, the federal government turned the area into a subsistence homestead colony.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beauxart_Gardens%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 205‑acre tract that became Beauxart Gardens housed 50 families, each with a house and several acres of land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beauxart_Gardens%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before the colony, residents of nearby Nederland and Viterbo used the land for intensive rice farming.",
